                                "sense_id": "72b88991-cf41-3e1c-85ab-7bb8b88b4cc6",
                                "text": "1892, Arthur Conan Doyle, The Adventure of the Cardboard Box,\nIt was a very long street of two-story brick houses, neat and prim, with whitened stone steps and little groups of aproned women gossiping at the doors."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b656d0be-625a-4601-ba35-8456a8f6883b",
                                "sense_id": "72b88991-cf41-3e1c-85ab-7bb8b88b4cc6",
                                "text": "1892, Arthur Conan Doyle, The Adventure of the Blue Carbuncle,\nHolmes pushed open the door of the private bar and ordered two glasses of beer from the ruddy-faced, white-aproned landlord."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4cb96deb-8310-4b79-aed1-e2e15a7f68c0",
                                "sense_id": "72b88991-cf41-3e1c-85ab-7bb8b88b4cc6",
                                "text": "The corridor was alive. Clusters of aproned figures mixed and disengaged."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "87877eb8-0678-421b-8e29-42aff7ec094b",
                                "sense_id": "72b88991-cf41-3e1c-85ab-7bb8b88b4cc6",
                                "text": "Together they contemplate the picture: the young wife with the daring clothes and gaudy jewellery striding through the front door, impatiently sniffing the air; the husband, colourless Mr Right, apronned, stirring a pot in the steaming kitchen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
